From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000068 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Veloce PDFium Patches <veloce-pdfium@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Make RenderPlan spatial culling fail closed

The spatial candidate mask introduced by 0066 made the spatial index an
authority for excluding path nodes, but index construction did not prove that
every node was represented. Empty, non-finite, or otherwise unindexable bounds
were silently omitted. RenderPlan segment bounds used the same optimistic
union rule. A tile could therefore report success while missing objects that
the later full-scan replay restored.

Make the culling contract explicit and conservative:

* Every path node is represented by one or more bins or by the always-replayed
  overflow list. Bounds that cannot be indexed are never silently dropped.
* Spatial queries include overflow nodes even when the regular grid query does
  not intersect the index bounds.
* Query clips are expanded by one device pixel before inverse transformation,
  matching PDFium's outward-rounded device intersection behavior at tile
  boundaries.
* A RenderPlan PathRun receives a skippable aggregate bbox only when every
  object in that run contributed finite, non-empty bounds. Any uncertain
  object disables segment-level skipping for that run.

Invariant: acceleration may exclude an ordered object only after proving that
its conservative painted bounds do not intersect the device tile. Uncertain
geometry remains on the existing replay path. This preserves painter order and
does not add any bitmap, cache, UI-thread work, or document-specific policy.

